          "block_order": 12
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "The two fundamental problems are $Ax=b and Ax=\\lambda x$ c for square matrices A. The fi rst problem $A x=b$ has a solution when A has independent columns. The second problem $A x=\\lambda x$ : looks for independent eigenvectors. A crucial part of this course is to learn what “independence\" means.\n",
          "block_bbox": [
            461,
            3441,
            2993,
            3789
          ],
          "block_id": 14,
          "block_order": 13
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "I believe that most of us learn fi rst from examples. You can see that ",
